You will join our Swiss immigration team in a permanent position, working on a flexible 80%-100% basis.
Our Swiss office is in Montreux, but the successful candidate may be based elsewhere in Switzerland. We particularly welcome applicants within reasonable reach of a major centre such as Geneva, Lausanne, Bern or Zurich.
The role offers significant flexibility and a combination of remote working and in-person collaboration.
You will manage your own matters with a high degree of autonomy, work alongside colleagues on more complex cases and contribute to the continued development of the Swiss practice.
This is a client-facing role. You will be expected to take responsibility for advising clients and progressing matters from the outset, rather than working primarily in a supporting capacity.
## **The Work** ##
Our Swiss immigration practice covers matters throughout Switzerland and across all cantons, including:
* EU/EFTA and third-country work and residence permits;
* corporate immigration and work authorisation;
* family reunification;
* residence for entrepreneurs, investors and financially independent individuals;
* private client immigration;
* settlement and C permits;
* Swiss citizenship and naturalisation;
* Schengen and national visas;
* cantonal and federal immigration procedures; and
* immigration appeals and other contentious matters.
Many of our cases involve wider questions of Swiss administrative law, taxation, employment or business structures, so experience in one or more of these areas can be particularly valuable.
## **What You Will Be Doing** ##

* advising private and corporate clients on Swiss immigration law, procedure and strategy;
* managing immigration matters from initial instruction through to conclusion;
* providing clear and practical advice directly to clients from the outset;
* preparing and reviewing applications, supporting evidence, legal submissions and correspondence;
* advising on work authorisation, residence rights, family migration, settlement and citizenship;
* identifying the immigration implications of corporate, employment, tax and private client arrangements;
* liaising with cantonal and federal authorities;
* advising on Swiss administrative procedures and, where appropriate, contentious immigration matters;
* identifying practical solutions to complex or unusual immigration issues;
* keeping up to date with developments in Swiss immigration law, policy and administrative practice;
* maintaining high standards of drafting, case management and client care; and
* contributing to the continued development and growth of Richmond Chambers Switzerland.

* a Bachelor's and/or Master's degree in Swiss law;
* full qualification as an Avocat in Switzerland and admission to a Swiss cantonal Bar;
* approximately 5-10 years of relevant professional experience;
* practical experience advising on Swiss immigration law or immigration-related matters;
* experience dealing directly with Swiss cantonal or federal authorities;
* sufficient technical experience to advise clients and take responsibility for matters from the outset;
* strong legal research, analytical and drafting skills;
* the ability to manage matters independently and exercise sound professional judgement;
* excellent organisational skills and attention to detail;
* strong interpersonal and client-facing skills;
* a pragmatic, commercially aware and solutions-focused approach; and
* a strong commitment to providing a high standard of client service.
This position is for a fully qualified Avocat. We are not considering applications on this occasion from avocats stagiaires, candidates who are still completing their professional legal training, or candidates who have not yet passed the relevant Swiss Bar examination.
We do not expect candidates to have spent their entire career practising exclusively in Swiss immigration law. We would be particularly interested in hearing from established Swiss Avocats whose practice has included meaningful immigration experience alongside another relevant area of Swiss law.
Experience in Swiss administrative law, taxation, employment law, corporate law or private client work would be particularly relevant.
## **Languages** ##
* Fluent English is essential.
* Fluent French is essential.
* Strong German-language skills would be a significant advantage, and Swiss German would be particularly welcome.
* Additional languages are also welcome.
## **Right to Work** ##
Applicants must have an unrestricted right to work in Switzerland at the time of application.
Unfortunately, we are not able to consider candidates who require sponsorship or new Swiss work authorisation for this position.
